.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-profile-create 1  "rev-stealth-config-profile-create " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-profile\-create \- Create a new profile directory and seed `policy.toml`, `authorized.toml`, and `sites/` via ConfigWriter (same skeleton as `config init`). Refuses if the profile already exists
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config profile create\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new profile directory and seed policy.toml + authorized.toml + sites/ via ConfigWriter (same skeleton as `config init`). Refuses if the profile already exists. Name must match [A\-Za\-z0\-9_\-]{1,64}.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Profile name. Must match `[A\-Za\-z0\-9_\-]{1,64}` (no `/`, `\\`, `.`, whitespace, control chars). Path\-traversal is rejected
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config profile create work
  $ rev\-stealth config profile create demo\-2026

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Profile created.
  1  UserError        Bad name / path traversal / already exists.
  3  PermanentError   ConfigWriter IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_PROFILES_ROOT   Override the profiles root directory.
